+# TLS Backend Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use Rustls as the TLS/SSL implementation. The recorded rationale is that Rustls has a smaller CVE history than the alternative that was previously in use, that it makes the implementation simpler, and that as a native Rust implementation of TLS 1.2/1.3 it avoids a C dependency chain and reduces the cryptographic attack surface.
